      "extract": "In the 60s and 70s Rochlin, Lickorish and Kirby established a remarkable connection between links and 3--manifolds. They showed that every 3--manifold can be obtained by surgery (on $S^3$) along framed links, and surgeries along two links give the same 3--manifold if and only if the links are related by a sequence of Kirby moves. This allows us to think of 3--manifolds as equivalence classes of framed links modulo",
